== Effects ==
* Adds a chance to shoot [[Petrification|petrifying tears]].
* {{dlc|nr}} +0.25 [[range]]. ({{dlc|na}} not applied until the next time Isaac's range stat is updated).
* {{dlc|r}} +1.5 [[range]].
* {{dlc|nr}} +0.5 [[tear falling speed]]. ({{dlc|na}} not applied until the next time Isaac's tear falling speed is updated).
* {{transformation contribution|Yes Mother?}}

== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|a+}} This item has a 1% chance to spawn when bombing {{m|Mom's Dressing Table}}. Multiple copies can be obtained through this method.{{dlc-}}
* Despite granting the [[Yes Mother?]] transformation, duplicated items will not contribute to unlocking Mom's Contacts. Three '''different''' items are required to unlock it.
* The chance to fire a petrifying tear depends on the [[luck]] stat, and the formula used to determine the chance is: <math>\min(\frac1 { 5 - \left \lfloor \mathit{Luck} * 0.15 \right \rfloor},50\%)</math>
** At base Luck (0), the chance is 20%, maxing out at 50% at 20 Luck.
* Petrifying the Heart of a {{E|Mask + Heart}} also freezes the Mask bound to it.
* Petrifying an enemy with a weak zone ({{E|Scolex}} or {{E|Carrion Queen}}) will make the enemy take damage anywhere while it is petrified, making combat significantly easier.

== Synergies ==
* {{i|Compound Fracture}}/{{i|Cricket's Body}}/{{i|Haemolacria}}/{{i|The Parasite}}: If the main tear causes petrification, split tears will too.
* {{I|Finger!}}: Finger can also apply the petrification effect.
* {{i|Lachryphagy}}: If freezing tears are fed first when they burst, the split tears can also freeze enemies.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Brimstone}}: The beam can occasionally freeze enemies with no visual difference.
* {{i|Epic Fetus}}: Occasionally fires missiles that can freeze enemies. No visual difference.
* {{i|Technology}}: Lasers can occasionally freeze enemies with no visual difference.
* {{i|Technology Zero}}: The electricity that is connecting tears has a chance to freeze enemies.

